		<id>https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/viewtopic.php?p=28824#p28824</id>
		<link href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/viewtopic.php?p=28824#p28824"/>
		<title type="html"><![CDATA[[FREE] Fantasy Dice (Android)]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/viewtopic.php?p=28824#p28824"><![CDATA[
This app makes use of <strong class="text-strong">3 different movement sensors</strong> and combines their data with a clever algorithm to create a stable, fast and accurate movement tracking system with your Android phone. When attached to <strong class="text-strong">Bullet physics modelling</strong> and HW accelerated 3D graphics, very compelling feel of control emerges where slight hand movements create immediate and natural looking visual feedback.<br><br>We have applied this technology to a dice app because it is a concept that everyone can understand and play with:<br><br><a href="http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_4-WkSyFrZE" class="postlink">http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_4-WkSyFrZE</a><br><br>In short: Movements of the device (an Android phone) are tracked with sensor fusion, and applied to a box that is visualized on the screen. A few dice move freely inside the box, handled by Bullet physics. Glass cover prevents them from bouncing out of the box.<br><br><img src="http://4.bp.blogspot.com/-UF7s_1-ZHJM/UGGYAidg6xI/AAAAAAAAAKc/kORfm9S1AO0/s400/Screenshot_2012-09-10-15-42-18_xoom.png" class="postimage" alt="Image"><br><br><img src="http://1.bp.blogspot.com/-X17t6uBYwyM/UGGX-TYWlvI/AAAAAAAAAKU/aU6IFIhBID4/s400/Screenshot_2012-09-03-11-59-52_xoom.png" class="postimage" alt="Image"><br><br>We are giving it away for FREE (and without advertisements), so if you have an Android device, download it from Google Play: <br><a href="https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=fi.finwe.fantasydice" class="postlink">https://play.google.com/store/apps/deta ... antasydice</a><br><br>Have fun with it! This is our first app with Bullet physics, so we're looking for your feedback.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=9584">finweltd</a> — Tue Sep 25, 2012 3:03 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
